# Copy this file to .env.local (already gitignored) and fill in real values.
# .env.local is never committed and only ever read on this machine / by
# Vercel's own env-var store -- never put real secrets in this .example file.

# --- Cloudflare R2 (api/uploadPresign.js) -----------------------------------
# Used by PhysioFeed's post composer to upload images/videos straight to R2
# instead of Supabase Storage (R2 has no egress fees). All five are also
# needed as REAL Vercel env vars (Project Settings -> Environment Variables)
# for this to work in production, not just local `npm run dev`.
#
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID, R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID, R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY:
#   Cloudflare dashboard -> R2 -> Manage R2 API Tokens -> Create API Token.
#   R2_ACCOUNT_ID is also shown on the main R2 overview page / Workers & Pages.
# R2_BUCKET_NAME:
#   The bucket you created (e.g. physiofeed-uploads). Defaults to that name
#   in code if this is left unset.
# R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL:
#   Cloudflare only shows you this AFTER you enable public access on the
#   bucket (Bucket -> Settings -> Public access) -- either the r2.dev dev URL
#   it gives you, or a custom domain if you attach one. No trailing slash.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET_NAME=physiofeed-uploads
R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=
